{"name": "dawnsbury", "game": "Dawnsbury Days", "version": "0.0.0", "hidden": false, "groups": [{"name": "Game Options", "options": [{"name": "progression_balancing", "display_name": "Progression Balancing", "description": "A system that can move progression earlier, to try and prevent the player from getting stuck and bored early.\n\nA lower setting means more getting stuck. A higher setting means less getting stuck.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "NamedRange", "default": 50, "min": 0, "max": 99, "presets": {"disabled": 0, "normal": 50, "extreme": 99}}, {"name": "accessibility", "display_name": "Accessibility", "description": "Set rules for reachability of your items/locations.\n\n**Full:** ensure everything can be reached and acquired.\n\n**Minimal:** ensure what is needed to reach your goal can be acquired.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "full", "display_name": "Full", "value": 0}, {"name": "minimal", "display_name": "Minimal", "value": 2}]}, {"name": "encounter_shuffle", "display_name": "Encounter Shuffle", "description": "Should the order of encounters within the campaign be randomized?", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": true}, {"name": "shuffle_level", "display_name": "Shuffle Level Restriction", "description": "When shuffling encounters, how many levels above an encounter's level can its replacement be?\neg, in \"Dawnsbury Days\", which goes from levels 1-4, if you set this to 3,\nyou can encounter the final boss (a level 4 encounter) as the first mission.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Range", "default": 0, "min": 0, "max": 20}, {"name": "include_free_encounters", "display_name": "Include Free Encounters", "description": "When encounters are shuffled, should we include the Free Encounters in the selection?\nIf so, should we include them only as padding for unfilled item drops, as randomly selected replacements for campaign encounters, \nadd some randomly chosen extras at each level, or increase the campaign length to include every possible encounter?\nNotes: \"Every Encounter\" might cause us to run out of drops, causing some encounters to not reward anything,\n         and no padding might cause us to run out of encounters, causing drops to stack up at the end of a level module.\n         By default, neither of these should happen if you have either (but not both) of item bonuses or basic locked actions enabled.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 1, "choices": [{"name": "none", "display_name": "None", "value": 0}, {"name": "as_padding", "display_name": "As Padding", "value": 1}, {"name": "as_replacements", "display_name": "As Replacements", "value": 2}, {"name": "some_extras", "display_name": "Some Extras", "value": 3}, {"name": "every_encounter_possible", "display_name": "Every Encounter Possible", "value": 4}]}, {"name": "include_extreme_encounters", "display_name": "Include Extreme+ Encounters", "description": "If we include free encounters, should we include Extreme+ (or harder) ones?\nCaution: Extreme+ free encounters often assume you have custom built characters, and may be *very* hard.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": false}, {"name": "extra_filler_amount", "display_name": "Extra Encounters Per Level", "description": "If we have selected \"Some Extra\" or \"Every Possible\" as the encounter setting, how many extra encounters should we add for each level?\nNote: the randomizer will try to add as many random encounters as you select here, but if the game runs out of unique random\n       encounters before we hit this number, the game will have to stack multiple drops onto the same encounter.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Range", "default": 2, "min": 0, "max": 20}, {"name": "loot_shuffle", "display_name": "Loot Shuffle", "description": "Should the encounter rewards (potions, scrolls, etc) be shuffled between encounters?", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": true}, {"name": "loot_randomizer", "display_name": "Loot Randomizer", "description": "Should the encounter rewards (scrolls, runestones, weapons, etc) be changed by the randomizer?\nYou can choose to make the new item match the original's type and/or level.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 1, "choices": [{"name": "do_not_randomize", "display_name": "Do Not Randomize", "value": 0}, {"name": "same_type_and_level", "display_name": "Same Type And Level", "value": 1}, {"name": "same_type", "display_name": "Same Type", "value": 2}, {"name": "same_level", "display_name": "Same Level", "value": 3}, {"name": "any_item_at_all", "display_name": "Any Item At All", "value": 4}]}, {"name": "mod_content", "display_name": "Include Modded Content", "description": "If you chose options which affect items, builds, or encounters, should the randomizer include modded content?\nWARNING: If enabled, changing which mods are installed during a run can cause issues.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": false}, {"name": "campaign", "display_name": "Campaign Selection", "description": "Select which campaign(s) you want to play.\nIf you include DLC, you must own that dlc or the campaign will not generate.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "dawnsbury_days", "display_name": "Dawnsbury Days", "value": 0}, {"name": "profane_barrier", "display_name": "Profane Barrier", "value": 1}, {"name": "dawnsbury_days_and_profane_barrier", "display_name": "Dawnsbury Days And Profane Barrier", "value": 2}, {"name": "good_little_children", "display_name": "Good Little Children", "value": 3}, {"name": "all", "display_name": "All", "value": 4}]}, {"name": "locked_actions", "display_name": "Locked Actions", "description": "If enabled, the archipelago will force you to unlock the 